      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>If you&#39;re considering Table-top RPGs, then I&#39;m looking to get Deadlands Noir and whatever companion books they have. My one friend borrowed my first copy so he could run a game, but he took it with him when he moved.</p><p>I bought my nephew &#39;Ghost Fightin&#39; Treasure Hunters&#39; for Christmas. He tried it at a local library event, and he really seemed to like it. The game looks great for playing with kids, but still fun for adults to play too.&nbsp;It wone an award in 2014 I think, and it seems to be so popular that they made&nbsp;a &#39;Ghostbusters&#39; re-skin of the game called &#39;Ghostbusters: Protect the Barrier&#39;.</p><p>&#39;Mysterium&#39; is cool, it plays something like Clue if you were playing it backwards... I&#39;d also like to maybe get Clue. Every game cabinet needs Clue(Or Clue-do, for our friends across the pond). Ah, and while we&#39;re talking about classics with a twist, &#39;Monopoly Gamer&#39; is super fun. And it doesn&#39;t make me want to kill the friend I&#39;m playing with...</p><p>There&#39;s &#39;Endangerd Orphans of Condyle Cove&#39;, &#39;Dracula&#39;s Feast&#39;, &#39;Are You Mental?&#39;... Wish I could give you more suggestions, but lots of what I want is either still on KS, &nbsp;or hasn&#39;t been released yet. :/</p>",
